    "created_at": "2023-10-16T00:57:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-16T00:57:45Z",
    "body": "> I think this goes a little to far in preventing the creation of a TextTrackCue with no cueFragment, which is important for those use cases where the purpose of using a cue object is to fire onEnter and onExit handlers. As I read it in this proposal, doing so would throw an InvalidNodeTypeError DOMException.\r\n\r\nRight, but you could provide just an empty, for example `<span cue cuebackground></span>`. That's not amazing, so yeah... tend to I agree.\r\n\r\n> I'm not sure the best document change to allow this, whether to explicitly allow the cueFragment to be null, or to support two constructors, one requiring cueFragment, the other with it absent.\r\n\r\nCan you help me understand that use case a little bit more?... I'm also leaning towards just allowing the `DocumentFragment` to be optional (would be equivalent to calling `new VTTCue(1,2, \"\")` ). \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
