    "created_at": "2023-10-16T09:30:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-16T09:30:08Z",
    "body": "> Can you help me understand that use case a little bit more?... I'm also leaning towards just allowing the `DocumentFragment` to be optional (would be equivalent to calling `new VTTCue(1,2, \"\")` ).\r\n\r\nThere are loads of use cases for this. Generically, anyone wanting to subclass `TextTrackCue` to add either metadata or time-based playback behaviour changes that don't involve adding HTML fragments to the shadow DOM attached to the `<video>`. E.g. adding HTML fragments to some other element on the page, like an indicator of the score during a sports video, or reactions, or \"here's an interesting fact about this thing that's happening right now\", etc etc.\r\n\r\nAssuming that the subclass has to instantiate the base class, the base class constructor needs to have the HTML fragment as an optional parameter. It's a small thing, especially in Ecmascript, but I'd lean towards allowing omission of the HTML fragment rather than specifying an empty string for it, just for cleanliness.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
