    "created_at": "2023-10-24T10:37:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-24T10:37:42Z",
    "body": "The rendering of WebVTT is currently specified as a custom non-CSS renderer of a non-DOM tree. I believe browsers have mostly implemented the rendering using CSS and DOM. I think they also don't follow the rendering requirements exactly, e.g. Safari has some padding on the background box and rounded corners, whereas the spec requires \"uglier\" background box without padding.\r\n\r\nMaybe this could be an opportunity to make the spec more aligned with implementations?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
